Scaled prefix V = d*{1..N-1}, threshold 1/N.  Live moduli & counts:
(comparing to primitive d=1 whose only live modulus is q=N with phi(N) live)

  N=4 d=1  V=[1, 2, 3]
    live (q,count): [(4, 2), (8, 2), (12, 2), (16, 2)]
  N=4 d=2  V=[2, 4, 6]
    live (q,count): [(8, 4), (16, 4), (24, 4), (32, 4)]
  N=4 d=3  V=[3, 6, 9]
    live (q,count): [(4, 2), (8, 2), (12, 6), (16, 2), (20, 2), (24, 6), (28, 2), (32, 2), (36, 6), (40, 2), (44, 2), (48, 6)]

  N=6 d=1  V=[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    live (q,count): [(6, 2), (12, 2), (18, 2), (24, 2)]
  N=6 d=2  V=[2, 4, 6, 8, 10]
    live (q,count): [(12, 4), (24, 4), (36, 4), (48, 4)]
  N=6 d=3  V=[3, 6, 9, 12, 15]
    live (q,count): [(18, 6), (36, 6), (54, 6), (72, 6)]

======================================================================
HONEST CONDITION: the clean live law liveCount=phi(N)*[N|q] holds for the
PRIMITIVE prefix (gcd=1).  With common factor d, live multipliers appear at
q not divisible by N (the dilation folds resonances).  Difference-closure is
necessary-not-sufficient; the exact condition is PRIMITIVE PREFIX {1..N-1}.
======================================================================

Enumerate all finite diff-closed subsets of {1..8} with gcd 1 (should all be prefixes):
  (1,)  prefix=True
  (1, 2)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3, 4)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7)  prefix=True
  (1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)  prefix=True

  => 8 primitive diff-closed sets in [1,8]; all prefixes: True
